    <statement><p>Find an equation of a plane containing the line
<m>\mathbf r = \langle 3, -3, 5\rangle + t
\langle -1, -6, 3\rangle</m>
which is parallel to the plane <m>3x + 1y + 3z = 16</m> in
which the coefficient of x is 3.</p>
<p><fillin characters="60" name="AnSwEr0001"/> = 0.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3\mathopen{}\left(x-3\right)+1\mathopen{}\left(y-\left(-3\right)\right)+3\mathopen{}\left(z-5\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
